      "level": 1,
      "content": "Theta Mathematics"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, let's dive back into the mathematical interaction of Theta."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Given the following function,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "f(n) = 4n + 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "let's find c1 * g(n) and c2 * g(n) based on the same conditions as before."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "c1∗g(n)≤f(n)≤c2∗g(n)c1 * g(n) \\leq f(n) \\leq c2*g(n)c1∗g(n)≤f(n)≤c2∗g(n)n≥n0n \\geq n_0n≥n0​c1>0c1 > 0c1>0c2>0c2 > 0c2>0n0≥1n_0 \\geq 1n0​≥1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Solution"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the growth of the f(n) function won't be faster than the c2 * g(n) function or slower than the c1 * g(n) function after n_0 because the above conditions are satisfied:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Since c1 * g(n) always grows slower than f(n), g(n) can be any expression such as 2n, 3n, etc. However, c1 * g(n) cannot be 10n, 12n, 4n, etc. because these functions grow faster than 4n + 3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Since c2 * g(n) always grows faster than f(n), g(n) can be any expression such as 5n, 10n, etc. However, c2 * g(n) cannot be 2n, 3n, etc. because these functions grow slower than 4n + 3."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Idea Emoji",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's assume c1 * g(n) is 2n and c2 * g(n) is 10n. In this scenario,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "c1∗g(n)=2nc1 * g(n) = 2nc1∗g(n)=2nc2∗g(n)=10nc2 * g(n) = 10nc2∗g(n)=10nf(n)=4n+3f(n) = 4n + 3f(n)=4n+3Since, f(n) cannot grow faster than c2∗g(n) and slower than c1∗g(n)Since,\\ f(n)\\ cannot\\ grow\\ faster\\ than\\ c2 * g(n)\\ and\\ slower\\ than\\ c1 * g(n) Since, f(n) cannot grow faster than c2∗g(n) and slower than c1∗g(n)2n≤4n+3≤10n [for all n≥1]2n \\leq 4n+ 3 \\leq  10n\\ [for\\ all\\ n \\geq 1]2n≤4n+3≤10n [for all n≥1]"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Theta Example",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As c1 * g(n) <= f(n) <= c2 * g(n) we can say that:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "f(n) = θ(g(n))\n=> f(n) = θ(n) [read as f(n) is Theta of n]"
    },
